F. SWITCHBOARD SYNTHESIS
==============================================================================================================================
  Tournament Analysis is not just extracting a tournament; it is choosing a switchboard.
  A switchboard has one comparator channel per unordered pair and a fixed tie-break path.

  rank shadows:     transitive states 172/172
  analyzer shadows: transitive states 31/672
  analyzer mean live edges per path: 22.95

  human dictionary:
    basketball pass-flux       = directed social energy
    reciprocity switch         = symmetric pair intensity toggles a base playbook path
    circle/sphere phase        = chirality, a tournament-native geometric relation
    annulus/resonance switch   = arbitrary metric banding on each pair
    dominant-axis lens         = cuboid pair chooses its own coordinate judge
    KL-skew lens               = simplex information geometry gives an asymmetric edge
    LRC safe-distance switch   = pairwise moat relation beside the marked lonely bracket

  working principle:
    rankers summarize objects; switchboards summarize relations.
    If the problem lives in pairwise tension, the switchboard is closer to the object.
